From a9dee93d74899b10040c065ada42e5a898a54465 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 06:03:49 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] rtrafd: the conntrack pass is paced by its own cost, and the
 health count shares it

Field (RT-BE88U): with a LAN DHT crawler holding ~10.7k conntrack entries,
rtrafd re-read all of /proc/net/nf_conntrack every 2 s and sat at about one
core, mostly kernel time spent formatting lines. The pass interval now
follows the cheapest of the last three pass costs so the pass stays near 3%
of one core (2 s floor, 30 s ceiling, one log line per change), every rate,
staleness and grace figure uses the measured interval, and the connection
health probe counts inside the same pass instead of a second full read.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 release/src/router/rtrafd/rtrafd.c | 234 +++++++++++++++++++----------
 1 file changed, 158 insertions(+), 76 deletions(-)

diff --git a/release/src/router/rtrafd/rtrafd.c b/release/src/router/rtrafd/rtrafd.c
index 28dbfe981c..775a25d5dd 100644
--- a/release/src/router/rtrafd/rtrafd.c
+++ b/release/src/router/rtrafd/rtrafd.c
